{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117472","id":3403997644,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7K5OHM","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117472","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117472.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117472.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117472","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117472/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117472/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117472/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0cf9430e9ba87ab33cdbe3b7b9cc2625474d4054","number":117472,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Reduce temporary count for chained operators","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"GDScript uses temporary locations on the stack, e.g. as intermediate targets for operations.\r\n\r\nAt the moment those temporaries are managed in a stack like fashion. Meaning a temporary `B` which was reserved before a temporary `A`, also must be freed up before `A`.\r\n\r\nThis approach is not great for chained binary operators `a + (b + c)`. Since the result of an operation needs to be handed out it needs to be reserved before the operands are calculated (since the operands have a shorter lifetime than the result). This keeps the result temporary reserved while the operands are calculated and forces chained binary operators to create new temporaries.\r\n\r\nThis PR changes temporary management to be able to free up any temporary at any time. This allows to only reserve the result of an operator after operands were calculated. So temporaries from those calculations can be reused.\r\n\r\nE.g. for a chain `p0 + p1 + p2 + p3 + p4 + p5 + p6 + p7 + p8 + p9`\r\n\r\nBytecode before:\r\n```\r\n 2: operator stack(21) = stack(3) + stack(4)\r\n 11: operator stack(20) = stack(21) + stack(5)\r\n 20: operator stack(19) = stack(20) + stack(6)\r\n 29: operator stack(18) = stack(19) + stack(7)\r\n 38: operator stack(17) = stack(18) + stack(8)\r\n 47: operator stack(16) = stack(17) + stack(9)\r\n 56: operator stack(15) = stack(16) + stack(10)\r\n 65: operator stack(14) = stack(15) + stack(11)\r\n```\r\nBytecode after:\r\n```\r\n 2: operator stack(13) = stack(3) + stack(4)\r\n 11: operator stack(14) = stack(13) + stack(5)\r\n 20: operator stack(13) = stack(14) + stack(6)\r\n 29: operator stack(14) = stack(13) + stack(7)\r\n 38: operator stack(13) = stack(14) + stack(8)\r\n 47: operator stack(14) = stack(13) + stack(9)\r\n 56: operator stack(13) = stack(14) + stack(10)\r\n 65: operator stack(14) = stack(13) + stack(11)\r\n```\r\n\r\n(GDScript operates under the assumption, that the result of variant operators can not overlap with the operands. I don't know if that is actually the case due to lack of documentation.)\r\n\r\nThis reduces the stack size of some functions. A reduced stack size reduces call overhead from setting up/tearing down the stack.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Benchmarked using this script</summary>\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node\r\n\r\nvar iter : int = 1_000_000\r\nvar test_strick : float = 0.0\r\nvar time : float = 0.0\r\n\r\nfunc add10(p0: int, p1: int, p2: int, p3: int, p4: int, p5: int, p6: int, p7: int, p8: int, p9: int) -> int:\r\n\treturn p0 + p1 + p2 + p3 + p4 + p5 + p6 + p7 + p8 + p9\r\n\r\nfunc add2(p0: int, p2: int) -> int:\r\n\treturn p0 + p2\r\n\r\nfunc noarg() -> int:\r\n\treturn v0\r\n\r\nvar v0 := 0\r\nvar v1 := 1\r\nvar v2 := 2\r\nvar v3 := 3\r\nvar v4 := 4\r\nvar v5 := 5\r\nvar v6 := 6\r\nvar v7 := 7\r\nvar v8 := 8\r\nvar v9 := 9\r\n\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tfor ii in range(1):\r\n\t\tvar sum: int\r\n\t\tvar func_10_t: float\r\n\t\tvar in_10_t: float\r\n\t\tvar func_2_t: float\r\n\t\tvar in_2_t: float\r\n\t\tvar func_no_t: float\r\n\t\tvar in_no_t: float\r\n\t\ttime = Time.get_unix_time_from_system()\r\n\t\tfor i:int in range(iter):\r\n\t\t\tsum += add10(v0, v1, v2, v3, v4, v5, v6, v7, v8, v9)\r\n\t\tfunc_10_t = Time.get_unix_time_from_system() - time\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\ttime = Time.get_unix_time_from_system()\r\n\t\tfor i:int in range(iter):\r\n\t\t\tsum += v0 + v1 + v2 + v3 + v4 + v5 + v6 + v7 + v8 + v9\r\n\t\tin_10_t = Time.get_unix_time_from_system() - time\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\ttime = Time.get_unix_time_from_system()\r\n\t\tfor i:int in range(iter):\r\n\t\t\tsum += add2(v1, v2)\r\n\t\tfunc_2_t = Time.get_unix_time_from_system() - time\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\ttime = Time.get_unix_time_from_system()\r\n\t\tfor i:int in range(iter):\r\n\t\t\tsum += v1 + v2\r\n\t\tin_2_t = Time.get_unix_time_from_system() - time\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\ttime = Time.get_unix_time_from_system()\r\n\t\tfor i:int in range(iter):\r\n\t\t\tsum += noarg()\r\n\t\tfunc_no_t = Time.get_unix_time_from_system() - time\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\ttime = Time.get_unix_time_from_system()\r\n\t\tfor i:int in range(iter):\r\n\t\t\tsum += v0\r\n\t\tin_no_t = Time.get_unix_time_from_system() - time\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\tprint(\"Args, Function, Inline, Overhead\")\r\n\t\tprint(10, \", \", func_10_t, \", \", in_10_t, \", \", func_10_t - in_10_t)\r\n\t\tprint(2, \", \", func_2_t, \", \", in_2_t, \", \", func_2_t - in_2_t)\r\n\t\tprint(0, \", \", func_no_t, \", \", in_no_t, \", \", func_no_t - in_no_t)\r\n\t\t\r\n\tget_tree().quit()\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nFor the function with a long chain of operators I see a reduction in call overhead of around 6%.\r\n\r\nI see a slight performance decrease only for the function with 2 arguments. However since this PR does not touch the VM and the bytecode of the function is not changed by this PR, I'm assuming this is some sort of cache shenanigans or code locality stuff.\r\n\r\n~Also I benchmarked using a debug build. Variance is too high for release. Might be worth a try to increase the iteration count and see whether the results become meaningful in release builds.~\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url